WEBVTT

00:06.006 --> 00:08.008
[opening theme music playing]

01:49.109 --> 01:56.074
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE

01:58.118 --> 01:59.994
[unsettling music playing]

02:00.078 --> 02:01.204
[man 1] How many casualties?

02:01.287 --> 02:04.541
[man 2] Three soldiers and another four
in Disease Control were killed.

02:04.624 --> 02:06.626
One major was seriously injured, sir.

02:06.709 --> 02:09.587
And it appears that most
of the Joseon test subjects died.

02:13.675 --> 02:15.677
[woman sobbing]

02:36.489 --> 02:38.533
[sobbing continues]

02:49.627 --> 02:51.629
- [Kato] How beautiful was it?
- [soldier whimpers]

02:51.713 --> 02:53.214
How'd it move around?

02:54.340 --> 02:56.217
Did you get to see how fast it was?

02:56.301 --> 02:58.303
[breathing shakily]

02:59.888 --> 03:01.848
- [mysterious music playing]
- [Kato] Go on. Tell me.

03:01.931 --> 03:04.309
- I wanna know everything that you saw.
- [soldier whimpers]

03:04.392 --> 03:05.476
Huh?

03:12.025 --> 03:16.779
6 HOURS EARLIER

03:22.869 --> 03:24.537
[unsettling music playing]

03:36.591 --> 03:37.967
[loud clattering]

03:38.843 --> 03:40.678
[air hissing]

03:43.223 --> 03:44.557
[hissing subsides]

03:47.977 --> 03:49.646
[tense music playing]

04:31.896 --> 04:33.898
[muffled growling]

04:44.325 --> 04:45.493
[soldier 1] Excuse me, Major.

04:45.576 --> 04:48.121
There are no more spores.
They've all disappeared, sir.

04:55.295 --> 04:57.088
[blood squelching]

04:57.171 --> 04:58.172
[gasps]

05:01.384 --> 05:02.385
[coughing]

05:03.011 --> 05:05.054
[labored breathing]

05:13.187 --> 05:14.772
[groaning, grunting]

05:14.856 --> 05:17.775
[gunshots]

05:18.484 --> 05:21.237
- [distant gunshots]
- [distant screaming]

05:27.368 --> 05:29.370
[elevator clatters]

05:33.291 --> 05:34.542
[elevator thuds]

05:39.881 --> 05:42.675
[breathing heavily]

05:42.759 --> 05:44.010
I need help!

05:45.678 --> 05:46.971
Somebody help me!

05:48.431 --> 05:52.226
[soldier 2 grunts, screams]

05:52.810 --> 05:55.229
Lights on! Hurry! Now!

05:55.313 --> 05:56.356
[soldier 3] Aim!

06:09.786 --> 06:11.537
Have you got a visual?

06:11.621 --> 06:13.539
[soldier 4] No, sir. I can't see anything.

06:25.593 --> 06:27.929
[muffled murmuring]

06:28.930 --> 06:30.932
[muffled murmuring continues]

06:32.558 --> 06:33.976
[soldier 5, muffled] Please help me.

06:37.105 --> 06:39.315
Please, somebody help me.

06:44.487 --> 06:45.613
Help me!

06:46.155 --> 06:47.740
[clear] I don't wanna die here.

06:48.282 --> 06:50.910
[whimpers] I can't die!
I don't wanna die here! Help, please!

06:51.661 --> 06:53.246
Shut that door right now.

06:54.789 --> 06:56.290
[whimpering]

06:57.750 --> 06:58.835
[groans]

07:01.796 --> 07:04.590
You better shut that door, now!

07:08.219 --> 07:10.138
[soldier 5 sobs, whimpers]

07:23.651 --> 07:25.153
[loud squeak]

07:28.531 --> 07:30.032
- [major] Why'd you stop?
- [whimpers]

07:30.116 --> 07:32.034
Shut it! Do it, or I'll shoot!

07:34.036 --> 07:37.498
Listen to me and shut it! Do it!

07:38.207 --> 07:40.334
[whimpers, sobs]

07:44.881 --> 07:46.257
- [loud thud]
- [anxious breathing]

07:49.635 --> 07:50.761
[whimpers]

07:52.180 --> 07:54.432
- [screams]
- [tense music playing]

07:56.309 --> 07:59.061
Help me, sir! Help me, someone!

08:02.482 --> 08:05.443
[soldier 5 desperately screaming]

08:07.028 --> 08:10.072
I don't wanna die! Get this thing off me!

08:11.532 --> 08:13.534
Let go of the door,
or I'll pull the trigger!

08:13.618 --> 08:15.995
- I'll blow your brains out!
- I don't wanna die today!

08:16.078 --> 08:19.540
Just do something, sir!
I don't wanna die like this, Maj. Endo!

08:20.791 --> 08:22.418
- [Endo] Let go!
- [soldier 5] No!

08:22.502 --> 08:25.004
- [Endo] Let go!
- Help me! Please help me!

08:25.087 --> 08:28.174
- Let go of the door! Let go of the door!
- Please don't let me die!

08:28.257 --> 08:30.510
[grunting, groaning]

08:31.761 --> 08:33.304
[creature growls ferociously]

08:33.387 --> 08:34.347
[whimpering]

08:34.430 --> 08:35.264
[bones cracking]

08:37.308 --> 08:39.560
Let go! Let go!

08:39.644 --> 08:42.188
Maj. Endo! Don't do this!

08:42.271 --> 08:43.981
- [Endo] You bastard!
- [screaming]

08:46.651 --> 08:47.985
[grunts]

08:52.990 --> 08:54.992
- [blood squelching]
- [groans]

08:55.952 --> 08:58.162
[gasping]

08:59.830 --> 09:01.123
[anxious breathing]

09:03.918 --> 09:06.837
[screaming]

09:06.921 --> 09:08.047
[creature roars]

09:10.424 --> 09:12.051
[moans]

09:12.134 --> 09:14.136
[creature growls]

09:14.220 --> 09:16.472
[breathing heavily]

09:22.061 --> 09:24.063
[elevator clatters]

09:27.483 --> 09:29.819
[Endo groaning]

09:37.285 --> 09:39.495
[breathing heavily]

09:45.501 --> 09:46.752
Go on, answer.

09:48.129 --> 09:49.797
Tell me what happened down there.

09:50.840 --> 09:51.882
Did we succeed?

09:51.966 --> 09:54.010
[breathing shakily]

09:54.093 --> 09:55.803
No, sir. Please just…

09:58.556 --> 09:59.724
destroy it, sir.

10:02.393 --> 10:03.394
You've created…

10:04.103 --> 10:05.521
you created a monster.

10:05.605 --> 10:06.689
[sobs]

10:07.982 --> 10:09.191
It's a total failure.

10:10.651 --> 10:13.654
Please destroy that thing
before it's too late.

10:14.655 --> 10:16.449
That monster's going to…

10:17.283 --> 10:18.909
it's going to kill us all.

10:18.993 --> 10:20.494
[crying]

10:30.212 --> 10:31.756
You think that she is

10:33.174 --> 10:34.258
a failure?

10:35.301 --> 10:37.303
[soldier 5 groaning]

10:41.265 --> 10:42.350
[clattering]

10:43.017 --> 10:45.019
- [thud]
- [bones cracking]

10:54.570 --> 10:56.280
[creature growls]

11:01.035 --> 11:03.996
[loud thud]

11:08.709 --> 11:10.711
[creature roars ferociously]

11:13.923 --> 11:15.925
[solemn music playing]

11:20.262 --> 11:21.305
I see.

11:29.730 --> 11:33.067
GYEONGSEONG CREATURE
BETWEEN OBSESSION AND PERSEVERANCE

11:33.150 --> 11:35.736
EPISODE 3
SIGNAL

11:42.326 --> 11:43.327
[slurping]

11:49.709 --> 11:51.210
This tea is really quite fragrant.

11:53.295 --> 11:55.423
Well, you were the one
who gave this to me.

11:56.716 --> 11:59.802
Thanks to you,
I'm enjoying my tea rituals a lot more.

11:59.885 --> 12:03.180
You have been so good to me.
It means a lot, Master Jang.

12:03.764 --> 12:06.851
How are you adjusting
in regards to your new life in Joseon?

12:06.934 --> 12:10.062
Oh, I'm adjusting quite well,
thanks to your wonderful support.

12:10.146 --> 12:11.230
Thank you for asking.

12:23.033 --> 12:26.912
So, um, Ongseong Hospital
has been recently shut down. Did you hear?

12:27.663 --> 12:29.665
Do you know anything about that?

12:31.667 --> 12:32.668
Only a little.

12:34.295 --> 12:37.298
I heard there's some kind
of infectious disease that got out.

12:37.965 --> 12:39.550
It spread all through the hospital.

12:40.968 --> 12:44.597
I see. Well, my friend was admitted there,
and I've been worried for her.

12:45.222 --> 12:47.683
I was wondering
if you knew anyone inside the hospital,

12:47.767 --> 12:51.645
someone who might have more information
about when they will open again?

12:51.729 --> 12:53.606
That way I can pay my friend a visit.

12:54.106 --> 12:57.151
Myeong-ja. Is that the person
you're looking for?

13:01.071 --> 13:04.074
If it is actually her,
then it's better to forget about it.

13:14.335 --> 13:15.628
Someone once told me,

13:16.754 --> 13:19.548
"Desperation can drive men to do things
that they would otherwise avoid."

13:21.383 --> 13:23.761
Now I am that desperate man
sitting here before you,

13:23.844 --> 13:25.221
hoping for some miracle.

13:27.973 --> 13:31.018
All I'm asking for
is a little help, Lady Maeda.

13:31.727 --> 13:35.898
Just brush off my husband's empty threats,
won't you? Can't you do that?

13:36.482 --> 13:40.110
Normally, I would
if it was just a mere threat, yet

13:41.445 --> 13:43.113
I believe he means it this time.

13:44.865 --> 13:45.699
And so?

13:45.783 --> 13:48.869
So I intend to mean business, too,

13:50.246 --> 13:51.997
if I really want to survive this, ma'am.

13:52.706 --> 13:53.791
[pensive music playing]

13:53.874 --> 13:56.752
Yes, but the hospital's closed.
No one's being admitted.

13:56.836 --> 14:00.631
Even if you get in, you won't find
what you're looking for, I'm sure.

14:01.674 --> 14:05.594
Trust me, you'd be better served
finding another way.

14:06.804 --> 14:09.473
That's what I'd say as your friend.

14:19.483 --> 14:21.360
I need the hospital's blueprints.

14:21.443 --> 14:23.571
Contact my connection
at the governor's office

14:23.654 --> 14:25.739
and see if you can get
the best blueprints available.

14:25.823 --> 14:29.869
What's the point of getting the blueprint
if the hospital is shut down?

14:29.952 --> 14:32.580
Nobody's breaking in.
You some locksmith now?

14:32.663 --> 14:35.749
They boarded up the place.
Even the supply shipments can't get in.

14:35.833 --> 14:37.459
What makes you think you'll find a way in?

14:37.543 --> 14:40.004
All I asked was
for you to get them for me.

14:40.087 --> 14:41.672
What about the infectious disease?

14:42.381 --> 14:45.342
We have no idea what that disease is,
and I'm not too thrilled to get it.

14:45.426 --> 14:47.761
All right, I'll go alone, Mr. Gu.
You can stay here.

14:47.845 --> 14:49.722
What if it's all one big lie?

14:49.805 --> 14:52.516
What if the sleuth girl lied
and needs your help to find a way out?

14:53.100 --> 14:54.810
I mean, it's possible, isn't it?

14:54.894 --> 14:56.645
The hospital shut down.
There's no way out.

14:56.729 --> 14:58.272
There's some disease spreading in there.

14:58.355 --> 15:01.191
She figures she might as well tell us all
she found Myeong-ja, huh?

15:01.275 --> 15:02.526
And you totally fell for it!

15:07.156 --> 15:10.451
- You believe that's what she's doing?
- Honestly, yes. Think about it.

15:10.534 --> 15:13.829
How can Myeong-ja go inside a hospital
for Japanese military officials?

15:13.913 --> 15:15.664
There's no way
she would be allowed inside.

15:15.748 --> 15:18.584
Okay? I'd bet my entire fortune
I'm right about this!

15:18.667 --> 15:21.837
Ah, well, you're actually quite unlucky.

15:21.921 --> 15:22.796
What?

15:22.880 --> 15:24.798
Every card you've drawn at the table
is crap.

15:24.882 --> 15:26.425
Every bet you've ever made, you've lost.

15:26.508 --> 15:29.762
Your gambling ability is unbelievably bad.
It's the worst I've ever seen.

15:29.845 --> 15:31.722
When has that ever--
The worst you've seen ever?

15:31.805 --> 15:34.099
I know that Myeong-ja
is definitely in there.

15:34.183 --> 15:36.602
I spoke with Lady Maeda earlier,
and she told me.

15:37.186 --> 15:38.812
[Mrs. Nawol] Ishikawa's wife?

15:38.896 --> 15:42.107
Did she actually confirm that?
Myeong-ja is really inside?

15:43.734 --> 15:46.820
That's what she said?
Myeong-ja's in there? She said that?

15:46.904 --> 15:50.199
I'm going, Mr. Gu, okay?
I'm going to Ongseong Hospital by 10:00.

15:50.282 --> 15:51.992
I'll need my things ready by then.

16:08.592 --> 16:11.261
WE FOUND MYEONG-JA

16:11.345 --> 16:13.347
[soothing music playing]

16:14.264 --> 16:15.599
[nurse] Send some kind of signal

16:16.183 --> 16:18.435
to the hospital's east wing
by ten o'clock.

16:19.228 --> 16:22.356
Use smoke or something
that can be seen from very far away.

16:22.439 --> 16:24.608
You won't find
what you're looking for, I'm sure.

16:24.692 --> 16:26.860
- Just find and help everyone.
- [tense music playing]

16:27.569 --> 16:28.737
You have to find a way.

16:28.821 --> 16:31.281
You'd be better served
finding another way.

17:02.604 --> 17:04.732
So tell me, what is Jang Tae-sang up to?

17:04.815 --> 17:07.985
Well, uh, he has gone all over town
this morning, sir.

17:08.485 --> 17:09.319
The thing is…

17:09.403 --> 17:10.821
[cheerful music playing]

17:10.904 --> 17:11.905
[Ishikawa] What is it?

17:12.531 --> 17:14.783
[man] His route has been a bit strange.

17:18.704 --> 17:19.663
[Ishikawa] Mahjong?

17:20.914 --> 17:21.749
I win!

17:21.832 --> 17:22.708
[man] Yes, sir.

17:22.791 --> 17:26.420
He played mahjong for an hour at the store
owned by the Chinese immigrant, Mr. Wang.

17:29.214 --> 17:30.966
FIREWORKS

17:39.641 --> 17:41.268
[Tae-sang] The next round is double.

17:42.561 --> 17:43.395
Are you in?

17:44.188 --> 17:45.022
I am.

17:45.981 --> 17:47.066
[chuckles]

17:47.149 --> 17:48.067
[Ishikawa] And then?

17:49.234 --> 17:51.361
[man] He rode a rickshaw
around the streets

17:51.445 --> 17:53.155
for maybe half an hour or so.

17:54.865 --> 17:57.493
- So he just rode around for no reason?
- [man] Yes, sir.

17:57.576 --> 17:59.745
And after all that, he paid a visit to…

18:05.292 --> 18:07.461
- He went to a tailor?
- Correct, sir.

18:07.544 --> 18:09.588
It looked like
he was getting a new suit, sir.

18:09.671 --> 18:13.133
I'd like to get it in that new style
that has gotten quite popular.

18:14.384 --> 18:15.219
Yes, sir.

18:25.020 --> 18:27.439
Master Jang, this here
is American-made pure wool.

18:27.523 --> 18:29.274
It just came in from Tokyo.

18:30.067 --> 18:33.946
I'm thinking you might prefer
the second fabric option, sir.

18:40.494 --> 18:43.747
It was sent over from the Moonlight Bar
last night, Master Jang.

18:45.040 --> 18:46.500
[music fades]

18:48.085 --> 18:48.919
[chuckles]

18:55.717 --> 18:57.928
[man 1] I'm with
the afternoon cleaning crew.

18:58.011 --> 18:59.304
ONGSEONG HOSPITAL

18:59.847 --> 19:00.931
[soldier 1] Go ahead.

19:01.431 --> 19:02.391
Yes, sir.

19:12.609 --> 19:14.027
CLEANING SUPPLIES

19:21.535 --> 19:22.494
[knocking on door]

19:24.246 --> 19:26.248
[pensive music playing]

19:33.422 --> 19:34.756
[Chae-ok] You deliver the message?

19:34.840 --> 19:36.800
I passed it on to someone trustworthy.
Don't worry.

19:36.884 --> 19:39.344
I'm sure by now,
Master Jang has already received it.

19:40.262 --> 19:44.266
Chae-ok, are you completely certain
that this girl Myeong-ja is down there?

19:44.349 --> 19:45.851
According to everything I've seen, yes.

19:45.934 --> 19:47.895
- Actually, there's something I--
- Oh!

19:49.771 --> 19:50.898
Don't shoot him, Father.

19:52.316 --> 19:53.442
He's not Japanese.

19:53.525 --> 19:54.651
You sure?

19:54.735 --> 19:56.195
He's a Japanese soldier though!

19:56.278 --> 19:57.654
Uh, no, no, no! I'm not!

19:57.738 --> 19:59.364
I'm from Joseon, I promise.

20:00.574 --> 20:02.993
I'm not the, um, enemy. I'm one of you.

20:21.261 --> 20:22.846
[Mrs. Nawol] Now, let's take a look here.

20:27.517 --> 20:29.937
Uh, it's in good condition.

20:30.729 --> 20:32.314
It's just the model's fairly old.

20:32.397 --> 20:36.151
Yes, well, it was how my family
made a living for the past ten years.

20:36.902 --> 20:38.987
It helped send my eldest son
to medical school.

20:39.071 --> 20:41.823
The best offer I can give you for this
is about 90 won.

20:42.491 --> 20:45.744
- Still willing to pawn it?
- I don't need the money, actually.

20:45.827 --> 20:46.828
Instead,

20:47.955 --> 20:50.332
I'd like you to please find my son for me.

20:51.291 --> 20:54.253
My eldest son was in the service,
and then he became injured,

20:54.336 --> 20:57.673
and that's… when I lost all contact.

20:58.674 --> 21:02.135
I was in school studying medicine
when they drafted me into their army.

21:03.095 --> 21:05.597
Then, at Bonglim, in China,
I was injured in a firefight.

21:05.681 --> 21:08.517
After that, I was sent here
to Ongseong Hospital.

21:08.600 --> 21:11.812
And once I recovered, my new assignment
became disease prevention.

21:12.562 --> 21:13.397
What else?

21:13.480 --> 21:17.317
This hospital conducts human experiments
down in the basement, Father.

21:19.611 --> 21:22.072
I saw many of our own
get killed last night.

21:24.283 --> 21:26.118
You wouldn't believe
how many were murdered.

21:28.578 --> 21:30.247
[man 1] The killings were caused by…

21:33.375 --> 21:35.252
an anthrax contamination.

21:35.961 --> 21:38.130
[solemn music playing]

21:38.213 --> 21:40.882
At Bonglim, I witnessed the same horror.

21:42.551 --> 21:45.804
They wiped out an entire village
of innocent people using anthrax.

21:45.887 --> 21:47.889
[people painfully screaming]

21:50.475 --> 21:53.312
I can still remember their screams
like it was yesterday.

21:53.395 --> 21:55.522
[screaming continues]

21:56.106 --> 21:58.150
Those damn bastards!
How could they do this?

21:58.775 --> 22:01.111
[janitor grunts, sighs]

22:03.488 --> 22:06.491
Perchance, did you happen to see
a young man in his early twenties

22:06.575 --> 22:08.076
among the dead bodies?

22:08.160 --> 22:11.121
He's average height, and he's got
a black birthmark over his right ear.

22:11.204 --> 22:12.331
He's my brother.

22:14.791 --> 22:16.168
I wouldn't know, I'm sorry.

22:17.085 --> 22:19.463
I wasn't able
to examine any of the bodies.

22:20.630 --> 22:21.631
[sighs]

22:22.215 --> 22:25.761
Just so you know, there are many people
from Joseon downstairs in the basement.

22:26.386 --> 22:28.305
Myeong-ja was down there. I'm sure of it.

22:28.889 --> 22:31.016
[air hissing]

22:32.142 --> 22:33.268
[sniffles]

22:37.814 --> 22:40.400
[man 1] Don't move
until we finish sterilizing the area.

22:41.735 --> 22:44.446
It's dangerous,
so please stay where you are.

22:45.822 --> 22:48.283
You could die
just by making contact with anthrax,

22:48.367 --> 22:51.495
so don't move and stay in that corner
until everything is sterilized.

22:52.079 --> 22:53.038
Do you understand?

22:54.790 --> 22:57.292
[sobs] Oh, sir, I need you to help me.
I can't stay here.

22:58.377 --> 23:01.963
You have to send for Commissioner Ishikawa
at the police station. Hurry!

23:02.047 --> 23:03.715
He doesn't know I am in here.

23:03.799 --> 23:08.303
Can you tell him Myeong-ja is stuck here?
No, Akiko. Say that Akiko is down here.

23:08.970 --> 23:11.139
He'll pay you handsomely
if you go and tell him.

23:11.932 --> 23:12.849
Please.

23:13.934 --> 23:15.894
Help me. I can't stay here.

23:15.977 --> 23:19.398
Contact the commissioner.
He must know that I am down here, please.

23:19.481 --> 23:21.400
- [banging on bars]
- [gasps]

23:21.483 --> 23:24.736
[soldier 1] Be quiet!
Shut the door! Stay back!

23:30.534 --> 23:32.536
[soothing music playing]

23:37.916 --> 23:39.960
[man 1] But there was nothing
I could do for her.

23:41.044 --> 23:43.422
Because I was
in the same boat as her, you see.

23:44.548 --> 23:46.550
[unsettling music playing]

23:49.553 --> 23:50.554
[retches]

23:59.771 --> 24:00.897
What are you doing?

24:03.358 --> 24:04.484
[breathes heavily]

24:07.237 --> 24:09.281
You dirty Josenjing!

24:11.575 --> 24:12.701
[grunts]

24:16.496 --> 24:17.789
[grunts angrily]

24:17.873 --> 24:20.000
What's wrong with you?
You're disgusting! Huh?

24:21.376 --> 24:23.920
- [coughing]
- [groans]

24:24.796 --> 24:25.714
[coughing]

24:27.674 --> 24:29.384
- [grunts]
- [groans, coughs]

24:30.010 --> 24:31.511
You dirty Josenjing!

24:33.054 --> 24:34.389
[kicking continues]

24:35.182 --> 24:36.850
[groans, coughs]

24:40.937 --> 24:42.898
- [straining]
- [groaning]

24:44.399 --> 24:46.276
Eat your vomit, Josenjing!

24:48.820 --> 24:50.280
[groaning]

24:54.910 --> 24:56.870
[man 1] There was only one way to escape

24:58.079 --> 24:59.122
this living hell.

24:59.789 --> 25:01.791
[somber music playing]

25:05.670 --> 25:06.755
[breathes deeply]

25:07.547 --> 25:08.548
Mother…

25:12.135 --> 25:14.095
I pray that you'll forgive me for this.

25:16.515 --> 25:20.185
[trembling, sobbing]

25:22.562 --> 25:25.524
[choking]

25:31.446 --> 25:33.323
[coughing]

25:34.407 --> 25:37.369
[gasping, coughing]

25:44.209 --> 25:45.126
Don't be stupid.

25:46.378 --> 25:47.337
[gasps]

25:49.506 --> 25:51.383
[Chae-ok] If you're gonna
give up your life…

25:53.552 --> 25:55.428
you need to make sure that it counts.

25:58.390 --> 25:59.224
Don't waste it.

26:03.520 --> 26:04.479
[sobs]

26:08.483 --> 26:10.026
[crying]

26:15.657 --> 26:16.825
[sniffles]

26:33.216 --> 26:34.676
[music fades]

26:36.928 --> 26:37.929
Who is she?

26:39.306 --> 26:40.307
I don't know.

26:41.600 --> 26:44.185
I have no idea
who the woman in the drawing is,

26:45.270 --> 26:47.772
but I do happen to know who the artist is.

26:49.316 --> 26:50.400
He's Japanese.

26:52.527 --> 26:54.404
He's employed as a painter here.

26:55.113 --> 26:56.448
I believe

26:57.157 --> 26:58.533
his name was Sachimoto.

27:01.328 --> 27:02.746
[pensive music playing]

27:13.465 --> 27:14.591
[creature roars]

27:17.969 --> 27:19.971
[pensive music continues]

27:22.974 --> 27:24.392
[creature breathing heavily]

27:31.691 --> 27:32.734
[knocking at door]

27:33.777 --> 27:34.819
[door opens]

27:35.820 --> 27:36.780
[door closes]

27:44.579 --> 27:45.789
[music fades]

28:01.554 --> 28:02.889
[doctor] What are all these?

28:04.099 --> 28:05.975
Why are you drawing this ugly thing?

28:07.519 --> 28:08.520
Huh?

28:13.608 --> 28:17.570
Get me some information.
Who he works for, and where he lives.

28:18.446 --> 28:19.823
Do you like Chinese food?

28:20.865 --> 28:23.284
How about eight o'clock tonight
at Sahaeru Diner?

28:23.368 --> 28:24.369
[exhales]

28:25.078 --> 28:28.081
I apologize, but I'm afraid I cannot
have dinner with you tonight, Yeong-chun.

28:28.164 --> 28:30.709
Oh, you're mistaken.
It's not with me, Master Jang.

28:31.376 --> 28:32.669
It's with Sachimoto.

28:32.752 --> 28:35.171
I'm having dinner with him tonight
at Sahaeru.

28:36.005 --> 28:37.841
- At 8:00 p.m.?
- Yes, that's right.

28:38.425 --> 28:39.426
Don't be late, okay?

28:46.015 --> 28:47.934
[unsettling music playing]

28:48.017 --> 28:51.104
[doctor] I hear you're running
quite an interesting experiment in here.

28:51.771 --> 28:54.691
You've decimated
an entire platoon of our soldiers,

28:55.191 --> 28:58.278
along with countless
of our Joseon test subjects.

29:00.196 --> 29:03.825
Surely, the end value of this experiment
must be worth all the trouble.

29:05.160 --> 29:06.870
What do you mean by that, sir?

29:07.454 --> 29:10.957
Tokyo has been burned to ashes
from the recent bombings of our enemies.

29:11.458 --> 29:15.712
We are now in desperate need
of a very powerful and secret weapon

29:16.296 --> 29:18.631
that could really turn the war around
for us all.

29:20.508 --> 29:24.888
Why don't we use this creature down below
that you've created?

29:27.265 --> 29:29.350
I still need to do more trials first.

29:31.019 --> 29:33.938
We still need to test
the creature's cognitive abilities.

29:34.022 --> 29:36.816
At the moment, it is still unclear
whether or not the creature is

29:37.817 --> 29:39.944
a beast that can be fully tamed.

29:40.528 --> 29:42.781
You know, every living being in this world

29:42.864 --> 29:46.201
has the potential to surrender
and serve its true master.

29:46.284 --> 29:49.120
As you can already see
from what we've done here in Joseon.

29:56.920 --> 29:58.922
[low snarling]

30:01.800 --> 30:04.427
[hissing, squelching]

30:12.560 --> 30:14.437
[snarling]

30:17.440 --> 30:19.692
[growling]

30:21.736 --> 30:23.738
[low snarling]

30:25.907 --> 30:27.909
[elevator clattering]

30:31.329 --> 30:33.331
[music fades]

30:34.040 --> 30:37.502
I've gone as far as the second basement,
and the prison is right here.

30:37.585 --> 30:40.129
As for Myeong-ja,
she was kept in this area.

30:42.674 --> 30:43.550
How many guards?

30:43.633 --> 30:47.345
Oh, right. So they have a pair of guards
stationed about every ten meters or so.

30:48.179 --> 30:49.013
All armed, of course.

30:49.097 --> 30:51.933
Getting her out of there is going to be
as difficult as you getting in.

30:52.600 --> 30:53.643
With that said,

30:55.019 --> 30:56.271
if you do manage to get her out,

30:56.354 --> 30:58.940
well, how do you plan
on escaping the hospital, then?

31:03.736 --> 31:05.446
For the meantime,
let's wait in our positions

31:05.530 --> 31:07.115
until we get the signal from the outside.

31:07.198 --> 31:09.325
And as for you,
go back to your station for now.

31:10.451 --> 31:13.329
No, I don't wanna.
I'd rather stay here with all of you.

31:13.413 --> 31:15.081
If you're missing from your station,

31:15.164 --> 31:17.458
they will look for you,
and we'll all be in danger.

31:17.542 --> 31:19.377
We can't risk them
finding out about these two.

31:20.169 --> 31:23.214
If that happens,
all of our work here will be for nothing.

31:26.676 --> 31:28.303
Don't worry. We will all escape together.

31:31.097 --> 31:32.098
I give you my word.

31:34.642 --> 31:36.644
All right, then. I'll see myself out.

31:38.354 --> 31:39.314
Just don't…

31:41.774 --> 31:43.401
don't forget about me, okay?

31:53.036 --> 31:54.287
[sighs]

32:01.294 --> 32:03.546
- [pensive music playing]
- [door opens, closes]

32:06.674 --> 32:08.509
Any chance you're seeing what I'm seeing?

32:09.469 --> 32:11.512
- With this floor plan?
- I am.

32:12.597 --> 32:15.516
The layout is similar
to the underground lab in Manchuria.

32:15.600 --> 32:17.435
We have to help everyone while we can.

32:19.270 --> 32:22.106
Like we should've in Manchuria.

32:24.150 --> 32:27.153
There's a chance
the same thing could be happening here.

32:29.280 --> 32:31.407
Think of the horrible things
we witnessed in Manchuria.

32:31.491 --> 32:32.533
Listen, Chae-ok…

32:32.617 --> 32:34.452
What if it's all happening here too?

32:37.163 --> 32:39.540
Shouldn't we do
everything we can to stop it?

32:40.124 --> 32:41.167
[sighs]

32:43.086 --> 32:45.755
Let's first wait for the signal, okay?
And then we'll proceed.

32:51.552 --> 32:53.805
[distant chattering]

32:59.018 --> 33:01.270
[whimsical music playing]

33:11.489 --> 33:14.117
[sighs] We've been waiting here
for 30 minutes.

33:14.200 --> 33:16.160
Exactly who are you waiting for anyway?

33:16.703 --> 33:17.537
A woman.

33:18.037 --> 33:19.414
Really? A woman?

33:19.497 --> 33:21.332
Don't act surprised, tough guy.

33:22.000 --> 33:23.334
Oh! There she is.

33:32.760 --> 33:33.845
[Tae-sang scoffs]

33:35.138 --> 33:37.598
Good work today.
Go get yourself something to eat.

33:38.725 --> 33:39.892
[money rustling]

33:39.976 --> 33:40.935
[car door closes]

33:44.355 --> 33:45.857
[tram bell rings]

33:55.533 --> 33:56.534
[both grunt]

33:57.243 --> 33:58.202
Oh, I'm sorry.

33:58.703 --> 34:00.747
Well, well, look who it is.

34:01.330 --> 34:03.708
The master
of the House of Golden Treasure.

34:08.796 --> 34:11.716
Do you mind? I'm busy tonight.
I have somewhere important I need to be.

34:12.508 --> 34:14.594
Welcome, miss. It's right this way.

34:17.430 --> 34:20.016
[indistinct chattering]

34:27.732 --> 34:28.983
[chuckles]

34:29.067 --> 34:32.445
Shouldn't we first settle some,
uh, unfinished business?

34:33.946 --> 34:35.948
All right. Listen, how's this sound?

34:36.949 --> 34:40.828
You and I will sit down and discuss
what it is that you think I owe you

34:41.496 --> 34:42.580
first thing tomorrow.

34:44.165 --> 34:46.417
[grunts, groans]

34:48.669 --> 34:49.796
[people gasp]

34:49.879 --> 34:51.130
What the hell is…

34:52.173 --> 34:53.091
[car door opens]

34:55.718 --> 34:57.095
- Uh, you're back.
- [moans]

34:57.178 --> 34:59.430
Hey, you hungry? Just help yourself, then.

34:59.514 --> 35:01.099
Here. Joseon pancakes.

35:01.182 --> 35:02.225
Yes, sir.

35:03.476 --> 35:04.727
[people gasp]

35:05.561 --> 35:06.646
[man] Delicious.

35:07.313 --> 35:09.065
These are so good.

35:09.148 --> 35:11.192
The Josenjing sure know how to cook.

35:11.275 --> 35:12.235
Mmm.

35:13.277 --> 35:16.614
Do you, uh, think he'll be okay?
I'm just curious.

35:19.575 --> 35:20.743
[Tae-sang groans]

35:23.037 --> 35:23.913
Mori.

35:24.497 --> 35:28.042
You and me, we just observe.
We don't get involved in anything, okay?

35:28.835 --> 35:31.170
We observe, then report,

35:31.671 --> 35:32.922
and do what we're told.

35:33.422 --> 35:36.592
That's it. Nothing else. Hmm?

35:37.176 --> 35:39.011
- Yes, sir.
- [man] Go on, try a bite. Try it.

35:42.640 --> 35:44.559
[grunts, groans]

35:45.101 --> 35:47.061
[moans]

35:48.187 --> 35:50.523
[Tae-sang coughing]

35:50.606 --> 35:52.692
Hang on. Wait, wait.

35:52.775 --> 35:53.693
Wait a second.

35:53.776 --> 35:55.611
We can resolve this with some money.

35:56.404 --> 35:59.240
We don't need that.
Let's put that away, huh? No weapons.

35:59.323 --> 36:02.994
Let's settle this man-to-man.
Just tell me your price. Yeah, that's it.

36:04.203 --> 36:05.163
I want everything.

36:05.746 --> 36:06.747
You want everything?

36:08.666 --> 36:09.500
What?

36:09.584 --> 36:13.337
Turn over your precious pawnshop to me,
and I'll let you walk away.

36:14.589 --> 36:16.257
[laughing]

36:19.510 --> 36:23.222
All right, stop joking around.
I already told you I was busy tonight.

36:23.306 --> 36:26.392
I told you I have important business
to attend. I really can't be late.

36:26.475 --> 36:28.019
Will you look at that? Look!

36:28.102 --> 36:30.313
It appears I'm already late!
I better go now.

36:30.396 --> 36:32.315
[whimsical music playing]

36:32.398 --> 36:36.694
Hey, you should really consider
who is of more importance right now, huh?

36:36.777 --> 36:38.112
Listen, my apologies.

36:38.196 --> 36:41.073
It's just I'm not really looking
for anything serious.

36:41.157 --> 36:44.535
Also, why are you trying so hard
to be an important person in my life?

36:44.619 --> 36:46.579
- All right, Jang Dai-sang.
- It's Tae-sang!

36:47.663 --> 36:49.665
It's not Dai-Sang. It's Jang Tae-sang!

36:50.583 --> 36:51.792
Now say it properly!

36:54.378 --> 36:56.214
You must really wanna die tonight.

36:56.297 --> 36:57.298
[scoffs]

36:59.342 --> 37:00.301
Of course I don't.

37:01.344 --> 37:03.262
Though I've never been that fortunate,

37:03.846 --> 37:06.182
I still don't want
some bumbling idiot to do it either.

37:06.265 --> 37:07.600
You son of a--

37:07.683 --> 37:08.684
[yells]

37:09.644 --> 37:12.104
[tense music playing]

37:20.905 --> 37:21.906
[flesh tears]

37:23.282 --> 37:25.201
[breathing heavily]

37:26.327 --> 37:28.079
[music subsides]

37:43.302 --> 37:45.721
[tense music resumes]

37:49.475 --> 37:50.601
[blade clatters]

38:28.055 --> 38:29.015
[yells in pain]

38:46.657 --> 38:47.783
[man 2] Hey, you over there!

38:48.993 --> 38:50.202
[groans]

38:50.286 --> 38:51.537
What's going on?

38:52.371 --> 38:53.414
[groans] Officer,

38:54.498 --> 38:57.168
I… I am Jang Tae-sang

38:57.251 --> 38:59.337
of the House of Golden Treasure.

38:59.420 --> 39:03.132
These thugs are attacking me
for no apparent reason, sir.

39:03.841 --> 39:06.218
Please help me, Officer. [moans]

39:06.302 --> 39:09.430
We just needed to teach
this stubborn Josenjing here a lesson.

39:09.513 --> 39:12.641
Nothing to worry about.
You can go. Have a good night, Officer.

39:12.725 --> 39:14.643
Officer, don't go! They have weapons.

39:14.727 --> 39:17.271
Look here! They've got samurai swords.

39:17.355 --> 39:19.648
My life is in danger.
Please help me, Officer!

39:21.734 --> 39:24.653
Well, don't go too crazy tonight.
You have a good night.

39:25.237 --> 39:26.155
[man] Thank you, sir.

39:26.238 --> 39:29.283
Officer, but they wanna kill me!

39:29.367 --> 39:30.785
[chuckles]

39:30.868 --> 39:31.952
Did you see that?

39:32.620 --> 39:35.081
I can do whatever I want.
This is your reality.

39:35.790 --> 39:38.709
And you're nothing
but worthless trash with a lot of money.

39:39.794 --> 39:42.505
You're a pathetic, dirty

39:43.756 --> 39:47.343
Josenjing.

39:48.469 --> 39:49.637
That's all you are.

39:56.477 --> 39:57.436
Boss!

39:57.520 --> 39:58.521
[moans]

40:01.190 --> 40:02.149
You're right.

40:03.317 --> 40:05.569
This is what has become
of my beloved country.

40:07.655 --> 40:09.782
So why don't you just give us all a break?

40:10.866 --> 40:13.452
'Cause at the moment,
I'm already pissed off as it is.

40:27.675 --> 40:28.801
Oh, look!

40:29.593 --> 40:31.595
He's a resilient Josenjing.

40:31.679 --> 40:33.639
[man laughing]

40:35.307 --> 40:36.600
He's one tough cookie.

40:59.290 --> 41:00.458
[sighs]

41:07.590 --> 41:09.216
This won't do, Father.

41:09.300 --> 41:12.386
If we wait any longer, we're gonna risk
losing the cover we have at night.

41:12.470 --> 41:14.763
I'll take a look
to see what's happening out there.

41:14.847 --> 41:16.849
[tense music playing]

41:26.025 --> 41:27.943
[Chae-ok] If this is the same layout
as Manchuria,

41:28.027 --> 41:30.779
there should be a vent
that connects into the underground lab

41:30.863 --> 41:32.072
that would also--

41:32.156 --> 41:33.824
Connect to the rooftop.

41:57.848 --> 41:59.099
[both grunting]

42:02.478 --> 42:05.564
Chae-ok, please don't take
unnecessary risks.

42:05.648 --> 42:08.400
Get out if it becomes
too dangerous for you. You got that?

42:09.151 --> 42:10.486
I'll be right back, okay?

42:23.040 --> 42:25.042
[tense music continues]

42:57.533 --> 42:59.743
[breathing heavily]

43:00.411 --> 43:02.663
[soldier 1] Hurry up! Hurry up and move!

43:19.972 --> 43:21.348
Did you get the blueprints?

43:22.266 --> 43:24.018
Yes, I got them, just like he told me to.

43:24.101 --> 43:26.270
Are you sure about this, Mrs. Nawol?

43:26.353 --> 43:29.023
I feel like we're sending Master Jang
over to death's door, don't you?

43:29.106 --> 43:31.025
You must support him, Mr. Gu.

43:31.108 --> 43:32.943
After all, he is the one who employs us.

43:33.027 --> 43:34.153
[sighs]

43:34.820 --> 43:35.863
[door opens]

43:38.574 --> 43:39.658
Is Tae-sang upstairs?

43:39.742 --> 43:42.036
I'm sorry, he's not here.
What's the matter, sir?

43:42.119 --> 43:45.289
I'm in a hurry and need to see Tae-sang.
It's an emergency, all right?

43:45.956 --> 43:47.458
- I see.
- [door opens]

43:51.045 --> 43:54.214
- [Jun-taek] Tae-sang!
- Master Jang! What happened to you?

43:55.758 --> 43:56.759
[groans]

44:04.725 --> 44:06.018
[Jun-taek sighs]

44:11.106 --> 44:14.068
Please wait here for a second, sir.
I'm going to speak with Master Jang.

44:14.151 --> 44:15.069
Okay.

44:28.666 --> 44:29.667
[groans]

44:39.843 --> 44:41.845
[groaning]

44:58.028 --> 44:59.446
[footsteps approaching]

44:59.530 --> 45:02.616
I didn't realize sword fights
were still happening these days.

45:02.700 --> 45:04.785
Oh, for heaven's sake! What the--

45:04.868 --> 45:08.330
Which rotten bastards did this?
Who dares hurt our Master Jang, huh?

45:09.081 --> 45:11.083
Wait here, and I'll go
to the police station for you.

45:11.166 --> 45:13.836
Let's go to the hospital first.
Get the car ready.

45:13.919 --> 45:15.504
Yes, the hospital. Which one though?

45:16.088 --> 45:19.049
Did you find the blueprints?
Where are they?

45:19.133 --> 45:21.927
I found them for you, Master Jang.
Yes, I did. Got them all!

45:22.010 --> 45:24.096
- They're downstairs.
- Don't worry about the blueprints.

45:24.179 --> 45:26.306
We must find a hospital
for you first, all right?

45:26.390 --> 45:28.142
Yes! Um, the hospital, right.

45:28.225 --> 45:31.478
I'll be fine, don't worry.
Go get the blueprints for me, Mr. Gu.

45:31.562 --> 45:33.021
[sighs]

45:33.105 --> 45:36.150
That cut you have is much deeper
than you think. You need a doctor.

45:36.233 --> 45:37.401
[Tae-sang sighs]

45:39.903 --> 45:43.657
I haven't the time, all right?
I said I'd be down there by 10:00.

45:43.741 --> 45:45.033
Listen, stop.

45:45.117 --> 45:46.785
I need those blueprints in here right now!

45:46.869 --> 45:48.078
Tae-sang, just stop!

45:53.292 --> 45:57.379
Nothing is more important than your life.
Listen to what I'm telling you, huh?

45:58.672 --> 46:01.842
Myeong-ja isn't more important
than you needing to get to a hospital.

46:02.593 --> 46:04.011
You can't risk your life over that.

46:04.094 --> 46:06.138
- I'm going, okay?
- I don't want to hear it.

46:06.722 --> 46:09.933
No job is worth your life, Master Jang.
See a doctor. Do you understand?

46:13.729 --> 46:14.605
Yes.

46:15.189 --> 46:18.817
I don't have the time, all right?
Myeong-ja isn't why I'm doing all this.

46:20.235 --> 46:21.236
Okay?

46:22.738 --> 46:24.865
I'm doing this because those bastards
wanna bankrupt me

46:24.948 --> 46:26.533
and take everything I've built.

46:27.701 --> 46:30.829
They wanna claim everything as their own,
even if we worked hard for it.

46:30.913 --> 46:32.706
They have no shame whatsoever!

46:32.790 --> 46:34.917
Listen, they took everyone I love from me.

46:35.417 --> 46:36.919
They're powerful bastards, you know?

46:38.003 --> 46:38.879
So what?

46:38.962 --> 46:40.631
[gentle music playing]

46:40.714 --> 46:41.715
I don't care.

46:44.051 --> 46:46.136
I'm still not going down without a fight.

46:48.055 --> 46:50.224
I won't let them push me around anymore.
I won't!

46:50.307 --> 46:53.060
I don't care who I go up against
or whatever they bring to the table!

46:54.770 --> 46:56.563
I'm not running away. I'm not a coward.

46:56.647 --> 46:58.816
I'm not gonna let them
terrorize us anymore.

47:00.234 --> 47:02.778
I have a lot of fight in me,
more than they think.

47:02.861 --> 47:03.737
And you know it.

47:04.321 --> 47:05.155
I know.

47:06.824 --> 47:08.283
But you were stabbed tonight.

47:10.327 --> 47:13.247
The cut is serious.
Please go to a hospital, okay?

47:14.915 --> 47:17.084
Wounds like these
don't pain me, Mrs. Nawol.

47:18.502 --> 47:21.296
Open wounds like this
aren't the issue here.

47:24.258 --> 47:25.509
The issue is my pride.

47:32.307 --> 47:34.977
[melancholy music playing]

47:35.060 --> 47:36.895
[footsteps approaching]

47:53.495 --> 47:54.621
[music fades]

47:54.705 --> 47:56.206
Yeong-chun, why are you here?

47:58.000 --> 47:59.459
I'm sorry. I know it's late.

47:59.960 --> 48:03.463
It's just… there's someone
who wants to speak with you, Master Jang,

48:03.547 --> 48:04.798
and he's here.

48:08.135 --> 48:10.429
[footsteps approaching]

48:18.937 --> 48:20.939
[unsettling music playing]

48:30.157 --> 48:32.159
[music intensifies]

48:40.792 --> 48:43.086
Mr. Wang, open the door.

48:43.170 --> 48:44.838
It's Mr. Gu. Open the door.

48:45.380 --> 48:46.298
[knocking on door]

48:46.381 --> 48:47.341
Mr. Wang!

48:55.933 --> 49:01.355
LABORATORY

49:49.611 --> 49:51.196
[matches rustling]

49:59.371 --> 50:00.455
[music fades]

50:00.539 --> 50:01.707
[gasps]

50:05.419 --> 50:07.421
[unsettling music playing]

50:55.886 --> 50:57.888
[music intensifies]

51:00.390 --> 51:01.349
[gasps]

51:03.894 --> 51:05.896
[music fades]

51:05.979 --> 51:08.273
[breathing shakily]

51:20.911 --> 51:22.329
[rickshaw clattering]

51:25.749 --> 51:26.958
[soldier] Mr. Sachimoto.

51:28.293 --> 51:31.046
Hello. Good evening.
I was getting art supplies.

51:31.630 --> 51:33.840
I need help unloading.
Can he come in for a minute?

51:37.010 --> 51:39.096
It's just I have
a lot of art supplies, sir.

51:39.721 --> 51:40.722
I can't allow that.

51:40.806 --> 51:43.475
Outsiders are not allowed to enter
the hospital. Those are my orders.

51:48.230 --> 51:49.106
All right.

51:49.648 --> 51:52.609
So then, report it to Director Ichiro,
why don't you?

51:53.610 --> 51:54.444
Pardon?

51:54.528 --> 51:57.280
Director Ichiro told me
to buy all of this tonight,

51:57.364 --> 51:58.240
so just call him.

51:59.991 --> 52:04.079
You can tell the director yourself
that you are not allowing his things in.

52:04.746 --> 52:06.164
[sighs]

52:35.235 --> 52:37.237
Are you here to save all of us?

52:38.572 --> 52:39.531
What?

52:39.614 --> 52:42.868
[girl] I saw you
coming down from the vent.

52:44.202 --> 52:45.787
Can you please save us?

52:46.496 --> 52:49.332
Can you please get us out of here?
Can you?

52:50.750 --> 52:53.086
[jangling]

53:05.515 --> 53:07.517
[unsettling music playing]

53:32.292 --> 53:33.710
[footsteps approaching]

53:38.173 --> 53:39.841
Go on! Hurry! [grunts]

53:41.760 --> 53:43.637
[music intensifies]

53:47.140 --> 53:48.516
[grunting]

53:59.361 --> 54:00.654
[music fades]

54:07.535 --> 54:08.745
[light clattering]

54:31.768 --> 54:33.770
[tense music playing]

55:01.965 --> 55:03.008
[breathes deeply]

55:04.551 --> 55:05.468
[music intensifies]

55:05.552 --> 55:07.053
Those little bastards.

55:10.598 --> 55:11.766
[doctor groans]

55:12.267 --> 55:13.643
[tray clatters]

55:14.853 --> 55:15.854
[doctor groans]

55:18.231 --> 55:19.232
[blood squelches]

55:20.025 --> 55:22.068
[doctor gasping]

55:22.152 --> 55:23.695
[music subsides]

55:23.778 --> 55:25.780
[breathing heavily]

55:36.666 --> 55:38.251
[panting]

55:43.340 --> 55:44.257
[Tae-sang] Come on out.

55:44.341 --> 55:45.300
[Jun-taek grunts]

55:46.801 --> 55:48.762
[groans] Oh my goodness.

55:49.429 --> 55:51.514
[breathing heavily]

55:51.598 --> 55:53.558
I thought I was gonna suffocate in there.

56:00.648 --> 56:01.983
[Sachimoto] Over this way.

56:11.409 --> 56:13.411
[eerie music playing]

56:15.330 --> 56:17.082
[vehicle approaching]

56:17.582 --> 56:18.541
CLOSED

56:18.625 --> 56:20.377
[unsettling music playing]

56:25.757 --> 56:27.759
[music intensifies]

56:41.022 --> 56:42.565
[tense music playing]

56:42.649 --> 56:45.026
[clock ticking]

56:50.115 --> 56:52.158
[music swells]

56:53.243 --> 56:55.245
[music subsides]

56:56.538 --> 56:59.666
- [breathing heavily]
- [unsettling music playing]

58:00.435 --> 58:01.352
What's going on?

58:02.145 --> 58:04.147
Are you sure
this is where they said to meet?

58:04.230 --> 58:07.567
I'm pretty sure this is the only
cleaning supply room on this floor.

58:10.862 --> 58:11.946
The signal.

58:15.158 --> 58:17.410
I wonder if our timing was off
'cause the signal was late.

58:19.662 --> 58:21.956
[music intensifies]

58:30.673 --> 58:32.467
[distant laughter]

58:32.550 --> 58:33.635
[man 1] Whoo!

58:34.511 --> 58:36.804
[man 1] The night air in Joseon
is quite refreshing.

58:36.888 --> 58:38.473
- [man 2] Yeah!
- [man 1 laughs]

58:39.057 --> 58:40.391
[man 3] Let's drink here.

58:49.192 --> 58:52.362
Look at this. I found whiskey
in the storage room earlier.

58:52.445 --> 58:54.948
- [man 4] Ah!
- So I snuck it out. [laughs]

58:55.031 --> 58:55.907
Oh yeah!

58:55.990 --> 58:56.991
[laughter]

59:19.806 --> 59:21.099
[music fades]

59:21.891 --> 59:23.893
[unsettling music playing]

59:35.405 --> 59:36.781
[music fades]

59:47.875 --> 59:49.502
Hey, be quiet.

59:51.421 --> 59:53.423
[tense music playing]

01:00:05.393 --> 01:00:07.103
[music intensifies]

01:00:11.983 --> 01:00:13.693
Hold your fire! Don't shoot!

01:00:19.866 --> 01:00:21.784
Please don't shoot me. I'm unarmed.

01:00:22.410 --> 01:00:23.536
Who are you?

01:00:31.127 --> 01:00:32.462
[fireworks whistling]

01:00:44.891 --> 01:00:46.726
- [man 1] What is this?
- [man 2] Fireworks?

01:00:46.809 --> 01:00:48.227
[fireworks exploding]

01:00:53.107 --> 01:00:54.651
[surprised gasp]

01:01:12.960 --> 01:01:15.505
[tense music playing]

01:01:21.427 --> 01:01:22.553
[groans]

01:01:22.637 --> 01:01:23.805
[grunts]

01:01:44.617 --> 01:01:45.702
Chae-ok!

01:01:57.338 --> 01:01:58.297
[gunshot]

01:02:02.677 --> 01:02:04.971
[music swells]

01:02:05.054 --> 01:02:06.347
[music fades]

01:02:14.313 --> 01:02:15.398
[fireworks explode]

01:02:18.484 --> 01:02:20.153
[tense music playing]

01:02:22.488 --> 01:02:24.282
[soothing music playing]

01:02:45.720 --> 01:02:46.846
I'm really sorry.

01:02:48.848 --> 01:02:50.558
Can you forgive me for being late?

01:02:51.058 --> 01:02:53.060
[breathing heavily]

01:03:06.532 --> 01:03:08.659
Ah, will you look at that, huh?

01:03:09.368 --> 01:03:10.995
[firework explosions continue]

01:03:17.710 --> 01:03:18.753
[blows]

01:03:28.596 --> 01:03:30.348
It looks like they succeeded.

01:03:30.431 --> 01:03:32.350
I really hope that you're right.

01:03:34.685 --> 01:03:36.270
Luck is on our side tonight.

01:03:43.653 --> 01:03:45.613
[Ishikawa] No, I'm not sure
what's going on.

01:03:45.696 --> 01:03:47.698
Yes, of course.
Fireworks are illegal in Gyeongseong.

01:03:47.782 --> 01:03:48.991
Everyone knows that.

01:03:49.075 --> 01:03:50.993
Yes, sir! I'll find who did this,
and when we do,

01:03:51.077 --> 01:03:53.538
I'll be sure to report to you
as soon as possible, sir.

01:03:53.621 --> 01:03:54.497
Yes, sir!

01:03:56.165 --> 01:03:57.250
[phone clatters]

01:03:57.333 --> 01:03:59.752
I must go to the bureau now.
Prepare my things.

01:03:59.836 --> 01:04:00.837
[man] Yes, sir.

01:04:16.352 --> 01:04:17.812
Would you look at that?

01:04:19.230 --> 01:04:21.399
Where's Myeong-ja, huh? Did you find her?

01:04:22.066 --> 01:04:23.943
Your message said you found her,
so where is she?

01:04:26.362 --> 01:04:28.197
[Chae-ok] Okay, you can come out now.

01:04:30.658 --> 01:04:32.535
[fireworks explode]

01:04:53.681 --> 01:04:54.765
[man] Careful.

01:04:56.893 --> 01:04:57.852
There we go.

01:05:07.820 --> 01:05:09.071
[Tae-sang] Wait.

01:05:10.489 --> 01:05:11.324
Where's Myeong-ja?

01:05:11.908 --> 01:05:13.576
These kids are our first priority.

01:05:13.659 --> 01:05:16.329
What are you talking about?
Why do you have all these kids with you?

01:05:16.412 --> 01:05:18.080
If you get the kids out of here,

01:05:18.789 --> 01:05:20.041
I'll find her, I swear to you.

01:05:20.124 --> 01:05:22.168
[pensive music playing]

01:05:27.882 --> 01:05:29.884
[music intensifies]

01:05:36.849 --> 01:05:38.476
[music fades]

01:05:38.559 --> 01:05:40.394
You said you have
something for me to look at?

01:05:41.520 --> 01:05:42.563
Yes.

01:05:43.606 --> 01:05:45.608
[elevator clattering]

01:05:46.400 --> 01:05:48.402
[elevator thuds]

01:05:53.324 --> 01:05:56.035
[man 1] Move! Hurry up! Move!

01:06:06.796 --> 01:06:10.424
[prisoners breathing nervously]

01:06:14.303 --> 01:06:15.638
[prisoners gasp]

01:06:20.893 --> 01:06:23.479
[prisoners whimpering]

01:06:24.480 --> 01:06:25.690
[prisoner 1] What's going on?

01:06:28.567 --> 01:06:29.735
[prisoners whimpering]

01:06:31.112 --> 01:06:33.322
[creature roars ferociously]

01:06:33.406 --> 01:06:35.199
[blood squelching]

01:06:35.950 --> 01:06:38.869
[prisoners screaming]

01:06:38.953 --> 01:06:41.372
[tense music playing]

01:06:44.417 --> 01:06:47.211
My plan is to train that creature
to understand who its master is.

01:06:48.838 --> 01:06:50.464
Every time I ring the bell,

01:06:50.548 --> 01:06:53.050
It will respond
and know that I'm feeding it.

01:06:53.634 --> 01:06:56.554
It will know
whoever has the bell is its master

01:06:56.637 --> 01:06:58.097
and that it must obey.

01:06:58.639 --> 01:07:00.599
I will tame the beast.

01:07:00.683 --> 01:07:02.685
- [woman whimpering]
- [bell ringing]

01:07:07.940 --> 01:07:09.942
[woman crying, whimpering]

01:07:17.116 --> 01:07:19.118
[intense music playing]

01:09:08.561 --> 01:09:10.563
[music subsides]

01:09:59.737 --> 01:10:01.739
[dramatic music playing]

01:10:41.612 --> 01:10:43.781
[music fades]
